# Brief-quality loop state (local working notes, not project files)
.scratch/

# Scratch output from the reader-quality scripts — frozen corpora, audit dumps,
# re-extraction diffs. Regenerated by the commands in docs/briefing-quality-handoff.md,
# and never a project file: a measurement belongs in a report, not a commit.
tmp/

# Worktrees are full checkouts of this repository, made by `git worktree add` for
# parallel agents working on disjoint branches. A file inside one is a file in the
# tree as far as `git status` and `eslint .` are concerned, but it belongs to
# another session and is never this session's diff. Ignoring the directory
# fixes the cause rather than one symptom of it: the symptom was `eslint .`
# walking into a sibling's probe script and reporting its formatting errors as
# this branch's lint failure — a red gate naming the wrong cause. A fresh CI
# checkout has no worktrees at all, so the runner never sees these; only a
# developer machine does. `git worktree add` is still the right way to make a
# baseline checkout, and `git worktree list` still shows them.
.worktrees/

# screenshots are local evidence only — never commit them
docs/screenshots/
